<Base title="Research" lang="en" description="Research projects, publications, and presentations related to PEP.">
  <div class="page-head"><div class="wrap"><p class="kicker">RESEARCH</p><h1>Research</h1></div></div>
  <article class="wrap prose">
    <p>PEP is built on the principle that research is education and education is research. Members of the PEP Research Group publish and present on project-based language learning, assessment, ICT in education, academic writing, and corpus linguistics.</p>
    <h2>Research projects</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Building a pragmatist framework for assessment in university English education (<a href="/research/eval-pragmatism/">details in Japanese</a>)</li>
      <li>A survey of students’ mobile devices and use of campus e-resources (<a href="http://itwp.pep-rg.jp/">Ritsumeikan University White Paper on Learning and ICT</a>, in Japanese)</li>
      <li>Visualizing assessment and establishing learning strategies in project-based English classes with digital badges</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Publications</h2>
    <p class="note">Titles are shown in their original language.</p>
    <Publications />
    <h2>Presentations</h2>
    <p class="note">Titles are shown in their original language.</p>
    <Presentations />
  </article>
</Base>
